# PostHog product analytics — set on the SERVER process, not in the browser bundle.
# The Rust backend reads PATOM_POSTHOG_KEY at startup and injects it into index.html
# so the SPA picks it up at runtime without a build step.
#
# For local dev: add PATOM_POSTHOG_KEY to your backend .env (or export it before
# running `cargo run`). Leave unset to disable analytics entirely — the SPA no-ops
# (OSS / self-host). Project API key from eu.posthog.com → Project settings.
#
# PATOM_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_...
# PATOM_POSTHOG_HOST=https://eu.i.posthog.com   # optional; this is the default
